(>> 4.1 Engineering Trusses and Determinacy Criteria) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A truss is an engineering structure composed of slender structural members joined) Tj
T*
(together at their end terminals to form a rigid stationary framework capable of spanning) Tj
T*
(large distances \(roof trusses, railway bridges, crane booms\).) Tj
T*
(* Classification by Internal Determinacy: Let m = total number of members, j = total) Tj
T*
(number of pin joints:) Tj
T*
(- Perfect \(Statically Determinate\) Truss: m = 2*j - 3. The truss is rigid and all member) Tj
T*
(forces can be uniquely solved using static equilibrium equations alone.) Tj
T*
(- Deficient \(Hypostatic / Unstable\) Truss: m < 2*j - 3. Lacks sufficient members to) Tj
T*
(prevent collapse under general loading.) Tj
T*
(- Redundant \(Statically Indeterminate\) Truss: m > 2*j - 3. Possesses redundant members;) Tj
T*
(cannot be solved by statics alone without deformation compatibility.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.2 Fundamental Assumptions in Plane Truss Analysis) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(To facilitate analytical solution, ideal truss analysis makes four classical) Tj
T*
(idealizations:) Tj
T*
(* 1. All members are connected at their ends by frictionless smooth spherical pins or) Tj
T*
(cylindrical hinges.) Tj
T*
(* 2. External loads and support reactions are applied strictly at the joints \(nodes\)) Tj
T*
(only.) Tj
T*
(* 3. The centroidal longitudinal axes of all members meeting at a joint are) Tj
T*
(concurrent at the joint pin center.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Self-weights of members are either negligible or split equally as concentrated) Tj
T*
(half-weights applied at end joints.) Tj
T*
(* Consequence: Every member is a pure two-force member carrying either axial Tension) Tj
T*
(\(T, pulling away from joint\) or axial Compression \(C, pushing toward joint\). Bending) Tj
T*
(moments and shear forces are zero.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.3 Zero-Force Member Identification by Inspection) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Structural efficiency is greatly expedited by identifying zero-force members prior to) Tj
T*
(numerical computation:) Tj
T*
(* Rule 1 \(Two-Member Joint\): If only two non-collinear members meet at an unloaded) Tj
T*
(joint without support reactions, the internal force in BOTH members must be ZERO: F1) Tj
T*
(= 0 and F2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(* Rule 2 \(Three-Member Joint\): If three members meet at an unloaded joint where two) Tj
T*
(members are collinear, the third non-collinear member MUST carry ZERO force: F3 = 0,) Tj
T*
(and F1 = F2.) Tj
T*
