(>> 4.5 Method of Sections) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(When internal forces in only a few specific internal members are desired \(e.g. central) Tj
T*
(chord or diagonal web members of a bridge\), the Method of Sections is far faster than) Tj
T*
(the Method of Joints:) Tj
T*
(* Step 1: Calculate global external support reactions.) Tj
T*
(* Step 2: Pass an imaginary cutting section through the truss, cutting the members) Tj
T*
(whose forces are required \(cutting through NOT MORE THAN THREE members whose forces) Tj
T*
(are non-concurrent\).) Tj
T*
(* Step 3: Isolate one side of the severed truss \(left or right\) as a non-concurrent) Tj
T*
(rigid body FBD.) Tj
T*
(* Step 4: Expose internal axial forces in cut members as external forces acting along) Tj
T*
(their member lines of action.) Tj
T*
(* Step 5: Apply non-concurrent planar equilibrium: Sigma M_joint = 0 \(taking moments) Tj
T*
(about the intersection of two unknown forces eliminates both simultaneously\), Sigma) Tj
T*
(Fx = 0, Sigma Fy = 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
