(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: In a roof truss, joint D connects horizontal chord CD, vertical web) Tj
T*
(member DF, and horizontal chord DE. Joint F has three members: vertical DF, and) Tj
T*
(diagonals CF and EF forming a symmetric V-shape. No external load acts at joint D.) Tj
T*
(Identify which member carries zero force and prove by joint equilibrium.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Examine Joint D:) Tj
T*
(Three members meet at joint D: CD and DE are collinear along the horizontal axis, and DF) Tj
T*
(is perpendicular \(non-collinear\). No external load or support reaction acts at D.) Tj
T*
(Applying Sigma Fy = 0 at joint D: DF is the ONLY member possessing a vertical component.) Tj
T*
(Sigma Fy = F_DF = 0. Hence, F_DF = 0 \(Zero-Force Member\).) Tj
T*
(Applying Sigma Fx = 0 at joint D: - F_CD + F_DE = 0 => F_CD = F_DE \(chord force is) Tj
T*
(continuously transmitted\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Member DF is a zero-force member \(F_DF = 0\). It serves purely to provide) Tj
T*
(lateral buckling restraint to the compression chord CD-DE.) Tj
T*
