T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: A symmetric Howe roof truss of span L = 12 m and height H = 4 m carries) Tj
T*
(a single ridge apex load P = 36 kN at joint C. Members are lower tie AB \(span 12 m with) Tj
T*
(central joint D\), rafters AC and BC \(length = sqrt\(6^2 + 4^2\) = 7.21 m\), and central) Tj
T*
(vertical tie CD = 4 m. Determine forces in all members.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Support reactions at A and B:) Tj
T*
(R_A = R_B = P / 2 = 36 / 2 = 18 kN \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Joint D Analysis:) Tj
T*
(Members AD and DB are collinear horizontally. Member CD is vertical. Unloaded joint.) Tj
T*
(By Rule 2: Force in central vertical post F_CD = 0 \(Zero-force member!\).) Tj
T*
(F_AD = F_DB = F_tie.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Joint A Analysis:) Tj
T*
(cos\(theta_A\) = 6.0 / 7.21 = 0.8321, sin\(theta_A\) = 4.0 / 7.21 = 0.5547.) Tj
T*
(Vertical equilibrium: R_A + F_AC * sin\(theta_A\) = 0 => 18 + F_AC * 0.5547 = 0 => F_AC =) Tj
T*
(- 32.45 kN \(Compression\).) Tj
T*
(Horizontal equilibrium: F_tie + F_AC * cos\(theta_A\) = 0 => F_tie = - \(-32.45 * 0.8321\) =) Tj
T*
(+ 27.0 kN \(Tension\).) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Rafters AC and BC = 32.45 kN \(Compression\); Bottom tie AB = 27.0 kN) Tj
T*
(\(Tension\); Vertical post CD = 0 kN.) Tj
